---
import MarketingLayout from '@/layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import Nav from '@/components/landing/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/landing/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Reflective Bootstrapping — Airic Research';
const description = 'How agents turn practice into institutional knowledge: reflection lenses, evidence-grounded proposals, and human review that governs learning and brings discoveries back to people.';
const stages = [
  { name: 'Practice', body: 'Act in the real world with existing knowledge.' },
  { name: 'Trajectory', body: 'Keep the actions, observations, and corrections.' },
  { name: 'Reflection', body: 'Interpret what the experience revealed.' },
  { name: 'Proposal', body: 'Identify a scoped change and its evidence.' },
  { name: 'Human review', body: 'Share the learning and decide what to adopt.' },
  { name: 'Incorporation', body: 'Make accepted knowledge available next time.' },
];
const mechanisms = [
  { title: 'Find friction', body: 'Retries, workarounds, repeated searches, and human corrections reveal gaps between expectations and reality. Informative successes can also teach.' },
  { title: 'Choose reflection lenses', body: 'Ask whether the episode reveals a workflow defect, missing context, a capability limit, or an authority conflict. Diverse precedents help expand the questions.' },
  { title: 'Form a Knowledge Delta', body: 'State what was learned, with quoted evidence, alternative explanations, scope, and uncertainty. Keep the conditions attached to the lesson.' },
  { title: 'Attribute the lesson', body: 'Identify which part of the operating model should change. A missing instruction, an instruction that was never loaded, and a tool defect need different responses.' },
  { title: 'Prepare an improvement proposal', body: 'Show the concrete revision, its intended effect, how future work will encounter it, and what would confirm or challenge it.' },
  { title: 'Improve reflection itself', body: 'Rejected proposals and later outcomes expose weak lenses or attribution habits. Changes to the learning method go through the same review process.' },
];
---

<MarketingLayout title={title} description={description} ogImagePath="/research-og-rb.png" ogType="article">
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <article>
      <header class="border-b border-border">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-muted-foreground">
            <span class="rounded-full border border-border-strong px-3 py-1.5">Airic Research</span>
            <span>October 2026 · Design proposal</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-10 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.4fr_0.6fr] lg:items-end">
            <div>
              <p class="font-mono text-sm text-muted-foreground">Practice → knowledge → institution</p>
              <h1 class="mt-4 text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.04] tracking-tight sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">Reflective<br />Bootstrapping</h1>
              <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">How agents turn practice into institutional knowledge.</p>
              <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                <a class="button-primary" href="#reflective-bootstrapping">Explore the learning loop <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
                <a class="button-secondary" href="#rb-skill">Get the RB skill <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
              <p class="eyebrow">The research question</p>
              <p class="mt-4 text-xl leading-snug">What can an organization inherit from the work its agents already do?</p>
              <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">A finished task is a deliverable. Its trajectory can also be the beginning of a better way to work.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="research-section" aria-labelledby="practice-heading">
        <div class="section-grid">
          <p class="eyebrow">01 · The intuition</p>
          <div>
            <h2 id="practice-heading">Practice produces knowledge.</h2>
            <p class="intro">We learn by doing. That familiar relationship continues when agents do the work.</p>
            <p>Instructions describe the world as their authors understood it. Contact with reality exposes hidden prerequisites, missing steps, local exceptions, and unstated expectations. Resolving those surprises produces new knowledge.</p>
            <p>The final deliverable rarely preserves what was discovered along the way. That knowledge remains in the trajectory, often unused by later tasks and unseen by the person who delegated the work.</p>
            <div class="mt-8 border-l-2 border-accent pl-6">
              <p class="text-xl font-medium leading-relaxed text-foreground">RB turns what an agent learns during work into improvements that people can understand, review, and keep.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="reflective-bootstrapping" class="research-section bg-secondary/35" aria-labelledby="loop-heading">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
          <p class="eyebrow">02 · The mechanism</p>
          <h2 id="loop-heading" class="mt-4 max-w-3xl">A learning loop grounded in real work.</h2>
          <p id="core-model" class="intro max-w-3xl">Reflective Bootstrapping is a governed process in which agents turn experience from practice into lasting improvements to their behavior, including improvements to how they learn.</p>
          <figure class="mt-10" aria-labelledby="loop-caption">
            <ol class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
              {stages.map((stage, i) => (
                <li class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
                  <div class="flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><span>{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><span aria-hidden="true">{i === stages.length - 1 ? '↺' : '→'}</span></div>
                  <h3 class="mt-5 text-lg font-semibold">{stage.name}</h3>
                  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{stage.body}</p>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ol>
            <figcaption id="loop-caption" class="mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Accepted changes guide the next round of practice. Review decisions, including rejections and corrections, become precedents for later reflection.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 border-t border-border pt-8 md:grid-cols-2">
            <div><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">What changes?</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The agent-facing operating model: instructions, procedures, quality criteria, skills, precedents, and paths to relevant guidance. The person reviewing a lesson also carries new knowledge back into the organization.</p></div>
            <div><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">What persists?</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Reviewed guidance and the reasons for adopting it. Later agents and colleagues can inherit a lesson without having taken part in the original task.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="reflection" class="research-section bg-secondary/35" aria-labelledby="reflection-heading">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
          <p class="eyebrow">03 · Reflection</p>
          <h2 id="reflection-heading" class="mt-4 max-w-3xl">From an informative episode to a reviewable change.</h2>
          <p class="intro max-w-3xl">Reflection lenses supply the questions. Evidence grounds the interpretation. Attribution identifies where a lesson belongs.</p>
          <div class="mt-10 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-8 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
            {mechanisms.map((item, i) => (
              <div class="border-t border-border-strong pt-5"><p class="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</p><h3 class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold">{item.title}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{item.body}</p></div>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6 sm:p-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Give each responsibility a suitable method.</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 max-w-4xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Reflection concentrates on meaning. Deterministic tools verify exact evidence spans, source versions, and edit preconditions. Smaller models may assist ambiguous lookup and routine routing. A text match can locate evidence; it cannot by itself establish historical provenance or causality.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="human-review" class="research-section bg-foreground text-background" aria-labelledby="review-heading">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
          <p class="eyebrow" style="color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-background) 65%, transparent)">04 · Human review</p>
          <h2 id="review-heading" class="mt-4 max-w-3xl">Review governs learning.<br />It also brings knowledge back to people.</h2>
          <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
            <div class="border-t border-background/25 pt-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Knowledge synchronization</h3><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-background/75">The agent explains what happened, what it learned, and where the lesson applies. The reviewer learns about discoveries hidden behind the deliverable and adds domain context that can correct or refine the interpretation.</p></div>
            <div class="border-t border-background/25 pt-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Accountable adoption</h3><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-background/75">People accept, narrow, defer, or reject a proposed change. A judgment deposit preserves the decision, rationale, evidence, scope, and accountable reviewer so future participants can understand and revisit it.</p></div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-10 max-w-3xl border-l-2 border-accent pl-6 text-xl leading-relaxed">The result is a reviewed change to the operating model and a better-informed person. An approval click alone does not demonstrate understanding.</p>
          <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-background/60">Permissions, audit mechanisms, and human-controlled constitutional constraints remain outside reflective modification.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="rb-skill" class="research-section" aria-labelledby="skill-heading">
        <div class="section-grid">
          <p class="eyebrow">05 · Put it to work</p>
          <div>
            <h2 id="skill-heading">Give your agent an RB skill.</h2>
            <p class="intro">Reflect on a completed task while the experience is still available, or use a saved trajectory.</p>
            <p>The skill guides the agent through Observe → Reflect → Attribute → Propose → Synchronize → Revisit. It produces evidence-grounded lessons and scoped changes for you to review.</p>
            <a class="button-primary mt-6" href="/research/rb-skill.md" download="SKILL.md">Download the RB skill <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
            <div class="mt-8 rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Start with the work you just did.</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Give the skill to an agent with access to the task context, then ask:</p>
              <blockquote class="mt-4 border-l-2 border-accent pl-4 text-base leading-relaxed">Use Reflective Bootstrapping to reflect on this task. Identify what we learned and prepare improvement proposals for my review.</blockquote>
              <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Review the evidence, interpretation, and scope before accepting persistent changes. Later work tests the lesson and can improve the reflection method itself.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm">A host system supplies trajectory capture and incorporation. The skill preserves uncertainty and human acceptance; empirical evaluation is pending.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</MarketingLayout>

<style>
  .research-section { padding-block: 5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); scroll-margin-top: 5rem; }
  .section-grid { max-width: 72rem; margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: 1.5rem; display: grid; gap: 2rem; }
  .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.6875rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--color-muted-foreground); }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.16; letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
  .intro { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-muted-foreground); }
  .section-grid > div > p:not(.eyebrow):not(.intro) { margin-top: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-muted-foreground); }
  .button-primary, .button-secondary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.75rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; padding: 0.875rem 1.125rem; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.35; }
  .button-primary { color: var(--color-background); background: var(--color-foreground); }
  .button-secondary { border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .button-primary:hover, .button-secondary:hover { opacity: 0.8; }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-foreground); outline-offset: 5px; }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) { .research-section { padding-block: 6rem; } .section-grid { grid-template-columns: 0.55fr 1.45fr; gap: 3rem; } }
</style>
